course: dictionary
lesson: 1191
title: Brushing: many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brushing is a word with several meanings, so the words around it are your best clue. «Brushing your teeth» means cleaning them with a brush and toothpaste. «Brushing your hair» means tidying it. In each case the words after brushing tell you what is being cleaned.
explain: «The leaves were brushing my face as I walked past.» Nobody is cleaning anything here. Brushing means touching something lightly as you pass. Swap in your meaning, "the leaves were touching my face lightly", and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Brushing can also mean putting paint, oil or egg on something with a brush, such as a cook brushing egg on a pie. The example sentence «Dad heard it and explained that a running tap can pour away several litres a minute — a bucket's worth in a couple of brushings» is harder, because the clues are about water. Ask what would fit, and check a dictionary if you are unsure.
fact: Brushing is the -ing form of brush, and it can also be a noun.
fact: «Brushing» can mean cleaning or tidying with a brush, as in brushing your teeth or brushing your hair.
fact: «Brushing» can mean touching something lightly as you pass, as in «the leaves were brushing my face».
fact: Brush your teeth twice a day, morning and before bed, for about two minutes with fluoride toothpaste.
fact: «Brush off» means ignore, and «brush up on» means practise again.
exercise: «The leaves were brushing my face as I walked past.» What does brushing mean here? | Shouting loudly | Painting with a brush | Cleaning with a brush | *Touching lightly as you pass
exercise: According to the lesson, how long should you brush your teeth? | *About two minutes | Only once a week | Until the toothpaste runs out | About twenty minutes
exercise: What does «brush off» mean? | Practise again | *Ignore | Clean very well | Paint over
test: What does «brush up on» mean? | Touch lightly | *Practise again | Paint with oil | Ignore
test: Why is brushing your teeth important? | It makes your teeth taste of fruit | Your hair grows faster | It stops you needing to sleep | *It removes plaque and bacteria that cause holes
exam: In «brushing the pastry with egg», what does brushing mean? | Hiding the egg under the pastry | Touching the pastry lightly | Cleaning the pastry with a brush | *Putting egg on the pastry with a brush
